    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds an `initials` field to the owner representation, computed as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo edits, following the existing `displayName` computed-field pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (which generates the `initials` accessor on `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that populates `initials` via:\n   ```java\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" +\n   owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n\nThe response is emitted by the existing `RespondWithOwner` OfficeFloor function through `ObjectResponse<OwnerDto>`, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `$.initials`. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `coreComputesInitials` acceptance test (`john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`).",
